---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&out.stdout)"
---
Search for datasets from the terminal.

dsk is the same program under a shorter name.

Usage: dataseek [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  search      Search every source at once, merged, deduplicated and ranked [alias: s]
  sources     List every source: what it covers, its protocol, its key, its docs
  bench       Time every source on real queries and measure their overlap
  inspect     Read a dataset page's metadata and the files it lists
  mcp         Serve search, sources and inspect to MCP clients over stdio
  cache       Show, warm or clear the cache
  doctor      Check the environment, keys and cache, and report readiness
  completion  Print a shell completion script to stdout
  man         Print the man page, in roff, to stdout
  help        Explain a command or a topic: environment, exit-codes

Options:
  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr; stdout data is unaffected

  -v, --verbose...
          Explain what is happening on stderr

      --json
          Emit JSON to stdout instead of text

      --color <WHEN>
          Colorize output (auto, always, or never)
          
          Possible values:
          - auto:   Color when stdout is a terminal and NO_COLOR is unset
          - always: Always color, even through a pipe (for `| less -R`)
          - never:  Never color
          
          [default: auto]

      --no-color
          Disable ANSI colors; shorthand for --color=never (or set NO_COLOR)

      --plain
          ASCII-only output; implies --color=never

      --no-progress
          No progress bars or spinners; status lines print plain, as in a pipe

      --cache-dir <DIR>
          Keep the cache here instead of the platform cache directory
          
          [env: DATASEEK_CACHE_DIR=]

      --connect-timeout <SECS>
          Seconds a host gets to accept the connection; each request's own deadline (15 s, 90 s for
          catalogs) still caps it. A host that misses a limit you set is not marked as down
          
          [env: DATASEEK_CONNECT_TIMEOUT=]
          [default: 10]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  dsk search sea surface temperature              every source, ranked
  dsk s mnist -s huggingface,kaggle               only these sources
  dsk s census --json | jq -r '.results[].url'    one field per line

Exit status: 0 success, 1 failure, 2 usage error, 130 interrupted.
`dataseek help exit-codes` and `dataseek help environment` say more.

Report bugs at https://github.com/lmarkmann/dataseek/issues
